# LAMMPS velocity-Verlet integration-failure case (Vigil LAMMPS case),
# written through the COEUS hermes plugin engine with a MEAN temperature
# trigger. Dilute LJ fluid, dt* = 0.05 (10x too large): temperature explodes
# from ~0.75 to >2e6 within ~6 steps, then LAMMPS aborts with "Lost atoms".
#
# The `dump custom/adios` reads adios2_config.xml in the run directory, which
# binds IO group "custom" to the hermes plugin. The dump (modified build)
# declares derive/V2mean = mean(|v|^2) = 3*T*; the engine's mean trigger fires
# on the super-heated step. x y z are dumped alongside vx vy vz so the flagged
# step can also be rendered (particle Fides model) on the SST render side.
#
# Run (writer side), after the clio runtime + CTE pool are up:
#   spack load iowarp@main adios2-coeus@vigil openmpi
#   cd test/real_apps/lammps
#   mpirun -n 1 /home/hxu40/software/lammps_bench/lammps/build/lmp -in in.lj_explosion_hermes

units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

lattice         fcc 0.5
region          box block 0 8 0 8 0 8
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0

pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5

velocity        all create 0.75 12345 dist gaussian
timestep        0.05
fix             1 all nve

# ADIOS dump through the hermes engine (IO group "custom").
# Columns: id + positions (render) + velocities (derive/V2mean = 3*T*).
dump            d all custom/adios 1 lammps.bp id x y z vx vy vz
dump_modify     d sort id

thermo_style    custom step temp ke etotal
thermo          1
run             6
